  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f:(0, \\infty) \\rightarrow(0, \\infty)$\r\n\r\n$f(x)=\\left|1-\\frac{1}{x}\\right|$ is not a function\r\n\r\n$\\because f(1)=0$ and $1 \\in$ domain but $0 \\notin$ co-domain\r\n\r\nHence, $f(x)$ is not a function.",
